<article class="env-remark" id="01DE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01DE">Remark <span data-tag="01DE">115.4.5</span> <span class="named">(Projective resolutions)</span>.</a>  Let $R$ be a ring. For any set $S$ we let $F(S)$ denote the free $R$-module on $S$. Then any left $R$-module has the following two step resolution </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  F(M \times M) \oplus F(R \times M) \to F(M) \to M \to 0.  \]
</div>
  <p> The first map is given by the rule </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  [m_1, m_2] \oplus [r, m] \mapsto [m_1 + m_2] - [m_1] - [m_2] + [rm] - r[m].  \]
</div>
</article>